# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this, every commit made on Windows prints a "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warning for each file it touches — 96 lines of it during the layout
# refactor — and diffs between contributors on different platforms can show
# whole files as changed when nothing was.
#
# text=auto lets Git decide what is text, and eol=lf pins what goes INTO the
# repository. Working copies still get the platform's native endings on
# checkout, so nothing changes for anyone editing on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
